$video2embedding — SigLIP 2 video embedding (averaged frames, base64 float16)

SUMMARY
  Samples frames from each videos[] file (default: ~5 frames per video), runs the
  same SigLIP 2 model as $image2embedding on each sampled frame, averages the
  768-d vectors, L2-normalizes, and writes one base64 float16 x256 embedding per
  video into embeddings[].

SYNTAX
  $video2embedding
  $video2embedding(every=10, gpu=True)
  $video2embedding(model='224', every=30)

INPUT
  videos[] — source video files (MP4, …)

OUTPUT
  embeddings[] — one base64 string per video (256-d float16, same format as $image2embedding)

ARGUMENTS
  every= — sample every Nth frame, 1-based (default: auto ~5 frames per video)
           if the video is shorter, uses the first frame
  model= — default (siglip2-base-patch16-384) | 224 | base-224
  gpu=   — use CUDA (default: on when torch sees a GPU; gpu=False for CPU)

MODELS
  Same as $image2embedding:
  Default: models/siglip2/google-siglip2-base-patch16-384/

DEPENDENCIES
  Uses .venvs/media (torch, transformers, Pillow, opencv-python).
  Run tools\setup_external_venvs.ps1 once, or: uv sync --extra video2embedding

ENVIRONMENT
  AH_EMULATE_VIDEO2EMBEDDING=1 — deterministic placeholder embedding, no model load.
  AH_VIDEO2EMBEDDING_GPU=0       — force CPU even when CUDA is available.

EXAMPLE
  @clip: $file('walk.mp4') -> $video2embedding(every=20) -> %vec%

PROMPT-CONSUMING
  No — videos[] pass through unchanged.
